  "notes": "Current Route91 Daughters of Jacob Bridge: full low blue plate-girder road deck, transverse floor beams and diaphragms, pale roadside barriers and outer rails, narrow raised verge walks, reinforced-concrete bank abutments and bearings, road center/edge markings. The separate tan lattice old bridge about130m north remains native context; it is not substituted for this crossing. Ordinary-picture exterior approximation. The public Jan2020 Yair SarfaTi panorama viewed south from the northern old crossing identifies the low blue road bridge and pale barriers; the older tan lattice photographs are excluded as primary geometry references. Current PMTiles and retained Q2916595/way30613435 control placement and signed axis. The source envelope includes short end abutments beyond the47.176m retained centerline. Width, plate-girder depth, floor-beam/bearing details and concealed bank foundations are approximate. No assertion of a surveyed engineering arrangement, no private photo textures, readable signs, vehicles or copied meshes. Native terrain is coarse; physical-device timing remains unmeasured. Native water follows the original standard terrain as river ribbons; no flat water plane or bespoke terrain is authored. The failed-load image preserves the original automatic crossing, including its existing steep eastern fallback/stub artifact. The authored-model view has graded, tested joins; no claim is made that the fallback artifact was fixed. No below-deck road crossing is mapped here, so no engineering road/rail clearance certification is claimed.",
